## 17. Authentication and Data Security

This is initially an owner-operated private application.

Requirements:

- Use Google Sign-In.
- Restrict access to the authorised owner account.
- Do not hardcode an invented email address.
- Provide a secure way to configure the owner's authorised Google account.
- Verify authorisation on the server for protected database operations.
- Never expose private OAuth tokens or credentials to the browser.
- Do not make the spreadsheet publicly editable.
- Do not allow unauthorised users to view, update, or delete expense records.
- Do not expose sensitive Google API error details to normal users.

Do not treat hiding a frontend button as access control.

