## 18. Important Business Logic

Implement these rules carefully.

1. Today's expense is calculated using the Asia/Kolkata timezone.
2. The default month is the current calendar month.
3. All reports must use actual saved data.
4. Daily expenses and bulk purchase line items must never be counted twice.
5. An unpaid expense still counts as an expense incurred, but not as money already paid.
6. Show incurred expenses, paid amounts, and outstanding amounts separately.
7. Partially paid expenses must display the correct remaining balance.
8. Editing a record must not change its unique ID.
9. Deactivated categories must remain visible in historical records.
10. Deleted records must not appear in active spending totals.
11. All calculations must be done accurately using numeric values.
12. All amounts must be displayed in Indian Rupee format, such as ₹1,25,000.00.
13. Handle missing data gracefully.
14. Refreshing the application must not erase saved records.
15. Do not silently save an expense when the database request fails.

